From 946f9df829aaa7a509efa08b57ee5c92b88d9bb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vignesh Sridharan <vignsrid@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Feb 2026 15:27:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] multi-vendor: Add vendor-specific TLV parsing support on
 receive path

Previously, the multi-vendor framework only supported adding vendor-specific
TLVs to outgoing messages (send path). This commit extends the framework to
support parsing vendor-specific TLVs on the receive path, providing symmetric
and complete vendor TLV handling.

Key changes:

- Added parser registration and execution infrastructure to multi_vendor
  * register_parser() for vendors to register parser functions
  * parse_vs_tlv() executes registered parsers for a message type
  * s_parsers array stores parser functions per message type

- Extended CmduMessageRx with vendor parser support
  * Added callback mechanism via setVendorTlvParser()
  * Added getTlvBuffPtr() to peek at TLV buffer without consuming
  * Added addVendorClass<T>() for parsers to add TLVs to message
  * Modified TLV_VENDOR_SPECIFIC handling to call vendor parsers first

- Implemented complete example in MultiVendorExample
  * parse_vendor_example_tlv() demonstrates OUI checking and parsing
  * Peeks at OUI, swaps bytes, compares before parsing
  * Returns nullptr if OUI doesn't match (allows other parsers)
  * Registered for AP_AUTOCONFIGURATION_SEARCH_MESSAGE

- Linked multi_vendor library to beerocks_controller
  * Enables vendor TLV parsing in controller

Architecture improvements:

- Callback-based design avoids circular dependency between tlvf and multi_vendor
- OUI checking delegated to individual vendor parsers (no framework-level OUI map)
- Iterator pattern: tries parsers in order, stops at first success
- Graceful fallback to generic tlvVendorSpecific if no parser handles TLV
- Symmetric with send path: same registration pattern for consistency

This completes the multi-vendor framework by providing symmetric send and
receive capabilities for vendor-specific TLV handling.

Signed-off-by: Vignesh Sridharan <vignsrid@qti.qualcomm.com>
